course: dictionary
lesson: 4337
title: Guano: a word from bats and birds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are new because they name things we rarely see. Context helps you work them out. «Bat droppings, called guano, pile into huge heaps that feed cave beetles and worms.» The words called guano tell you that guano is another name for bat droppings.
explain: Read on for more clues. The heaps feed beetles and worms, so guano is something living things can use. The sentence also says guano was once mined as valuable fertiliser. Mined means dug out of the ground, so people dug guano up because it was worth money.
explain: Now check your meaning. Swap it into the sentence: «Bat droppings, called bat droppings, pile into huge heaps...» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits. Good readers always do this check before they move on.
fact: Guano means the droppings of seabirds or bats.
fact: Guano piles up in huge amounts on rocks and in caves.
fact: Guano is full of nitrogen and phosphorus, which help plants grow, so it is used as a strong fertiliser.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «bat guano», «bird guano» and «guano islands».
fact: Guano was once very valuable, which is why some islands near Peru were important in history.
exercise: «Bat droppings, called guano, pile into huge heaps.» What does guano mean? | *The droppings of bats or seabirds | Small stones found in caves | Dried leaves from a tree | A kind of cave beetle
exercise: «Bat droppings, called guano, pile into huge heaps.» What do the words called guano tell you? | *Guano is another name for the droppings | Guano is a cave on an island | Guano is a bird that can fly | Guano is a kind of bat
exercise: Why is guano used as a fertiliser? | *It is full of nitrogen and phosphorus, which help plants grow | It smells sweet and attracts bees | It keeps plants cold in winter | It is hard like a rock and keeps plants safe
test: «Guano was once mined as valuable fertiliser.» What does mined mean here? | Thrown into the sea | Painted on a wall | *Dug out of the ground | Stored in a bag
test: Which of these is a phrase with guano from the lessons? | *guano islands | guano clouds | guano rain | guano wind
exam: Which is the best way to work out the meaning of guano in «Bat droppings, called guano, pile into huge heaps»? | Ignore the sentence and guess from the length of the word | *Read the words around it and swap your meaning into the sentence | Decide it must be a kind of plant | Skip the whole text and never come back to it
